Subject: [PATCH] Give shared register descriptor templates consistent identity

The pinned compiler 6a7a7c531f54baed1dddfda1b80299413c4c6943 declares
FieldTemplate, RegisterTemplate and DescriptorTemplate in an anonymous
namespace inside a shared header. Generated named register types inherit
these translation-unit-local bases. DMA composers and their callers therefore
disagree on the identity of the returned descriptor types.

Keep the templates in the existing named detail namespace. Preserve all
members, layout expressions and serialization logic. No warning is disabled.
Both freshly compiled NPU40XX/NPU50XX composer/caller pairs reproduce the
original failure with -Werror=odr during a partial LTO link.

--- a/src/vpux_compiler/include/vpux/compiler/dialect/VPURegMapped/descriptors.hpp
+++ b/src/vpux_compiler/include/vpux/compiler/dialect/VPURegMapped/descriptors.hpp
@@ -41,8 +41,6 @@
 namespace vpux::VPURegMapped::detail {
 
 std::pair<mlir::ParseResult, std::optional<elf::Version>> parseVersion(mlir::AsmParser&);
-
-namespace {
 
 constexpr auto FLOAT16_BIT_SIZE = sizeof(uint16_t) * CHAR_BIT;
 constexpr auto FLOAT32_BIT_SIZE = sizeof(float) * CHAR_BIT;
@@ -762,5 +760,4 @@
     return descriptor.hashValue();
 }
 
-}  // namespace
 }  // namespace vpux::VPURegMapped::detail
